 [[Cookbook:Slicing|sliced]]\n* 1 large can [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomato]]es\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] quick-cooking [[Cookbook:Tapioca|tapioca]]\n* 1 whole [[Cookbook:Clove|clove]] or ½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] ground cloves\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Bay Leaf|bay leaves]]\n* [[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]] to taste\n* [[Cookbook:pepper|Pepper]] to taste\n\n==Procedure==\n\n# Trim all fat from meat. \n# Put all ingredients in crockpot; mix thoroughly. \n# Cover and cook on low 12 hours or on high 5 to 6 hours.\n# Remove bay leaves before serving.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* You can use the cheapest beef in the market; it will get tender in the pot.\n\n[[Category:Inexpensive recipes]]\n[[Category:Slow cooker recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for stew]]\n[[Category:Recipes using beef]]\n[[Category:Recipes_with_metric_units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using carrot]]\n[[Category:Recipes using celery]]\n[[Category:Recipes using clove]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Crock Pot Beef Stew","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"2 pounds (900 g) stew beef, cut into 1-inch (2.5 cm) cubes","sourceText":"2 pounds (900 g) stew beef, cut into 1-inch (2.5 cm) cubes","amountText":"2 pounds (900 g) stew beef, cut into 1-inch (2.5 cm) cubes","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"5 carrots, cut into 1-inch pieces","sourceText":"5 carrots, cut into 1-inch pieces","amountText":"5 carrots, cut into 1-inch pieces","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 large onion, cut into chunks","sourceText":"1 large onion, cut into chunks","amountText":"1 large onion, cut into chunks","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"3 stalks celery, sliced","sourceText":"3 stalks celery, sliced","amountText":"3 stalks celery, sliced","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"1 large can tomatoes","sourceText":"1 large 